1 OCCU Graf von Nassau-Dillenburg, Regierender Graf von Nassau in Dillenburg (1504, 1516 - 1559)
1 TITL graaf
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willem_I_van_Nassau-Dillenburg '''Willem I van Nassau-Dillenburg'''] - Wikipedia =- Dutch ; [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=pv&GRid=44770594&PIpi=23448748 '''findagrav
2 CONC e...''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_I,_Count_of_Nassau-Dillenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT He was called William the Rich
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William I "the Rich" 1487-1559, Count of Vianden and Dietssz 1516-1559, Count of Nassau-Dillenburg 1544-1559
2 CONT
2 CONT William of Nassau (Dutch: Willem de Rijke) (10 April 1487– 6 October 1559). He was called William "the Rich". William was born in Dillenburg as the younger son of Count John V of Nassau-Dillenburg and landgravine Elisabeth of Hess
2 CONC e, daughter of Landgrave Henry III of Hesse-Marburg and Anna of Katzenelnbogen.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the brother of Count Henry III of Nassau-Breda and the father of the later William I of Orange-Nassau, who inherited the principality of Orange. The early House of Orange-Nassau (until 1702) descends from him, while the lat
2 CONC er House of Orange-Nassau (1702-1890) and the present Dutch royal family descends from his third son John VI "the Elder". William I was married twice :
2 CONT
2 CONT First he married October 29, 1506 Countess Walburga van Egmond (1490–1529). She gave him two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Elisabeth, 1515–1523
2 CONT     Magdalene, 1522–1567, married July,16 1538 to Count Hermann of Neuenahr and Mörs
2 CONT
2 CONT Second he married September 20, 1531 Countess Juliane of Stolberg-Wernigerode (1506–1580). They had twelve children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     William I (Maurice) "the Silent" of Nassau, born 25 April 1533, died 10 July 1584
2 CONT     Hermanna, born 9 August 1534, died young
2 CONT     John VI "the Elder", born 22 November 1536 – 28 October 1606
2 CONT     Louis, born 10 January 1538 – 14 April 1574, killed in fighting in the 80 Years War
2 CONT     Maria, born 15 March 1539 – May 1599, married on 11 November 1556 to Count Wilhelm IV of Berg-s'Heerenberg
2 CONT     Adolf, born 11 July 1540 – 23 May 1568, killed in fighting in the 80 Years War
2 CONT     Anna, born (21 September 1541 – 12 February 1616, married on 16 June 1559 to Count Albrecht of Nassau-Weilburg-Ottweile
2 CONT     Elisabeth, 25 September 1542 – 18 November 1603), married 16 June 1559 to Count Conrad of Solms-Braunfels
2 CONT     Catharina, born 19 December 1542 – 25 December 1624), married on 17 November 1560 to Count Günther XLI of Schwarzburg-Arnstadt
2 CONT     Juliana, born 10 August 1546 – 31 August 1588), married 14 June 1575 to Count Albrecht VII of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt
2 CONT     Magdalena, born 15 December 1547 – 16 May 1633), married on 27 January 1567 to Count Wolfgang of Hohenlohe-Weikersheim
2 CONT     Henry, born 15 October 1550 – 14 April 1574, killed in fighting in the 80 Years War
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Far	Johann V Graf von Nassau-Dillenburg,   f. 9 nov. 1455, Breda, The Netherlands ,   d. 30 jul. 1516, Dillenburg, Hessen, Germany   (Age 60 år)  Mor	Elisabeth Landgräfin von Hessen,   f. maj 1466, Marburg, Hessen, Germany ,   d. 
2 CONC 17 jan. 1523, Köln (Køln, Cologne), Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany   (Age ~ 56 år)  Gift	11 feb. 1482 
