2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Welf-24]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernst (Ernest I) Welf aka Guelf, Guelph, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernest of Brunswick-Lüneburg (German: Ernst der Bekenner) (1497–1546)[1], also frequently called Ernest the Confessor, was duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg and a champion of the protestant cause during the early years of the Protestant 
2 CONC Reformation. He was the Prince of Lüneburg and ruled the Lüneburg-Celle subdivision of the Welf[2] family's Brunswick-Lüneburg duchy from 1520 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Henry I, Duke of Lüneburg, and Margarete of Saxony, the daughter of Ernest, Elector of Saxony.
