1 OCCU Prins Willem "de Zwijger" ("The Silent") van Oranje, Graaf van Nassau (Stadtholder of the United Provinces of the Netherlands), Prince of Orange, Fürst von Oranien (1544 - 1584) Graf von Nassau, 1577 Generalstatthalter in den Nied
2 CONC erlanden
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''William the Silent''' was born on April 24, 1533 in Dillenburg, Giessen, Hesse, Germany. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-56368440 Willem I, Graf von Nassau-Dillenburg] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-56368509 J
2 CONC uliana, Gräfin zu Stolberg-Wernigerode]. He was a Prins Willem &quot;de Zwijger&quot; (&quot;The Silent&quot;) van Oranje, Graaf van Nassau (Stadtholder of the United Provinces of the Netherlands), Prince of Orange, Fürst von Oran
2 CONC ien (1544 - 1584) Graf von Nassau, 1577 Generalstatthalter in den Niederlanden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William I married [https://www.geni.com/profile-71491615 Anna van Egmont van Buren] on July 8, 1551 in Buren, Buren, Gelderland, The Netherlands. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34659417171 
2 CONC Maria van Nassau]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-67994606 Filips Willem van Nassau, prins van Oranje]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-86138029 Maria Van Nassau (Oranje-Nassau), Gräfin zu Hohenlohe-Neuenstein]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William I and [https://www.geni.com/profile-71748784 Eva Elinx] had an illegitimate son, whom William officially recognised and raised: [https://www.geni.com/profile-126739489 Justinus van Nassau Dillenburg (van Nassau)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William I married [https://www.geni.com/profile-72317028 Anna von Sachsen (Wettin, Albertiner), Prinzessin van Oranje-Nassau] on August 25, 1561 in Leipzig,Leipzig,Saxony. Together they had the following children: [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/profile-34668603935 Anna van Nassau (Nassau), Prinzessin]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-124025972 Anna van Nassau (Nassau), Gräfin zu Nassau-Dillenburg]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-124025957 Maurits van Oranje- Nassau (N
2 CONC assau), Prinz]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-72314809 Maurice of Nassau, Prince of Orange]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-33017394 Emilia van Oranje- Nassau]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William I married [https://www.geni.com/profile-72329214 Charlotte de Bourbon, prinses van Oranje] in 1575. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-39025649 Countess Louise Juliana Van Nassau (van O
2 CONC ranje- Nassau), Pfalzgräfin und Kurfürstin von der Pfalz]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37974645 Elisabeth van Nassau]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-72388398 Catharina van Oranje-Nassau (van Oranje- Nassau), Gräfin zu Hanau-Münz
2 CONC enberg]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-71743189 Charlotta Van Nassau, Abbess of Poitiers]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-72389416 Charlotte Brabantine van Nassau]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-27254706 Emilia Secunda &quot;Antwer
2 CONC piana&quot; van Nassau, prinses van Oranje]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William I married [https://www.geni.com/profile-71748783 Louise de Coligny, Fürstin von Oranien-Nassau] on April 24, 1583. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-9211572 Frederick Henry of Nassau, 
2 CONC Prince of Orange]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 10, 1584 in Delft, Delft, South Holland, Netherlands from Assassination by Balthasar Gérard and was buried on August 3, 1584 in Nieuwe Kerk, Delft, Delft, Zuid-Holland, Nederlande. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_the_Silent William the Silent in English Wikipedia]==
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''source''' : [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_the_Silent Willem the Silent]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William I 1533-1584 "the Silent", Count of Nassau, Vianden and Dietssz, Prince of Orange 1544-1584, Lord of Egmond and Count of Buren 1551-1584, Stadtholder of Holland, Zeeland, Utrecht and Burgundy, VisCount of Antwerp, Baron of 
2 CONC Breda 1559-1584, Stadholder of Brabant 1577, Stadtholder of Frisia 1580
2 CONT clclick the image to enlarge
2 CONT
2 CONT William I, Prince of Orange, also widely known as William the Silent (Dutch: Willem de Zwijger), or simply William of Orange (Dutch: Willem van Oranje),was born on 24 April 1533 in the castle of Dillenburg in Nassau, present-day G
2 CONC ermany.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the eldest son of William "the Rich", Count of Nassau and Juliana of Stolberg-Werningerode, and was raised a Lutheran. He had four younger brothers and seven younger sisters: John, Hermanna, Louis, Mary, Anna, Elisabeth, Ka
2 CONC tharine, Juliane, Magdalene, Adolf and Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT When his cousin, René of Châlon, Prince of Orange, died childless in 1544, the eleven-year-old William inherited all Châlon's property, including the title Prince of Orange, on the condition that he receive a Roman Catholic educat
2 CONC ion. He became Prince of Orange in 1544 and is thereby the founder of the branch House of Orange-Nassau. Besides Châlon's properties, he also inherited vast estates in the Low Countries (present-day Netherlands and Belgium). Becau
2 CONC se of his young age, Holy Roman Emperor Charles V served as the regent of the principality until William was fit to rule. William was sent to Brussels to study under the supervision of Mary of Habsburg (Mary of Hungary), the siste
2 CONC r of Charles V and governor of the Habsburg Netherlands (Seventeen Provinces). In Brussels, he was taught foreign languages and received military and diplomatic education and became a wealthy nobleman.
2 CONT --------------------
