2 CONT *'''Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg, Prince of Lüneburg reign''' 1559–1592, Until 1569 he ruled together with his brother [http://www.geni.com/people/Heinrich-I-Herzog-zu-Braunschweig-und-Luneburg/6000000001500248316 Henry(Heinrich)]
2 CONT >'''Predesessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000001500246498 Ernest I] '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000006727753438 Errnest II]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Welf-41]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm "der Jüngere, Herzog von Braunschweig in Lüneburg" von Braunschweig und Lüneburg formerly Welf
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm (Welf) von Braunschweig und Lüneburg is a member of aristocracy in Europe.
2 CONT Join: European Royals and Aristocrats 1500-Present Project Discuss: EUROARISTO Biography Wilhelm (1535–1592), called the Younger (German: Wilhelm der Jüngere) was the fourth son of Ernst I, Duke of Brunswick und Luneburg in Lunebu
2 CONC rg of the house of Welf, and his wife, Sophie von Mecklenburg, and was born 4 July 1535.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg and Prince of Lüneburg from 1559 until his death. Until 1569 he ruled together with his brother, Henry of Dannenberg.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 12 October 1561 he married Dorothea of Denmark (29 June 1546 Kolding–6 January 1617 Winsen), daughter of Christian III King of Denmark and his wife, Dorothea of Sachsen-Lauenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1582, William began suffering from fits of insanity. These fits caused his wife to flee him in 1584 for her own safety.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, his wife became regent for their son George.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Names William the Younger was a member of the House of Welf.[3] The Brunswick-Lüneburg name is probably more aptly referred to as a landed title.
