1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Countess_Louise_Juliana_of_Nassau
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise Juliana of Orange-Nassau (31 March 1576 in Delft – 15 March 1644 in Königsberg) was a countess consort of the Palatinate by marriage to Frederick IV, Elector Palatine, and took part in the regency government of her son betw
2 CONC een 1610 and 1614.[1] She also acted as a mediator between the king of Sweden and the elector of Brandenburg in 1631.
