1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00000088&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Countess Charlotte Brabantina of Nassau From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Countess Charlotte Brabantina of Nassau (Antwerp, 17 September 1580 - Château-Renard, August 1631) was the fifth daughter of William the Silent and his third spouse Charlotte of Bourbon. [edit]Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Countess Charlotte Brabantina, her sister Elisabeth and their stepmother Louise de Coligny went to Paris in 1593. Elisabeth married Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne, Duke of Bouillon and at that wedding Charlotte Brabantine met the Cla
2 CONC ude, Duc de Thouars, whom she married in 1598. The Duke died only six years later, leaving Charlotte Brabantina with a couple of young children.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had four children: Henry; Charlotte, who married James Stanley, Earl of Derby; Élisabeth (1601-1604); and Frédéric (1602-1642) comte de Laval. In 1602, Charlotte-Brabantine dissuaded her husband from engaging in the conspirac
2 CONC y of Biron and encouraged him to lend allegiance to the king. He died in 1604.
