1 NOTE {geni:about_me} An oil painting of her at the age of 17 has survived in Heidelberg. See "Städtische Gallerie auf dem Heidelberger Schlosse (Friedrichsbau), No.436 neuer, No.30 alter Katalog"<br/>
2 CONT Their wedding, on 25 Nov 1551,  was a huge celebration in the Castle of Heidelberg. Both the bride and bridegroom were close to the Kurfürst Friedrich II. Three events were combined in a lavish five day festivity: the wedding of t
2 CONC hese two, the wedding of Graf Philipps von Hanau and the 70th birthday of Kurfürst Friedrich II.<br/>
2 CONT She was buried next to her husband in the Jacobskirche, Höningen - the gravestone contains the shields of Leiningen, Zweibrücken, Westerburg and Schaumburg.<br/>
2 CONT
