1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaretha van Mechelen
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaretha van Mechelen (circa 1580, Lier – 17 May 1662, The Hague) was a South Dutch noblewoman and (from c.1600 to c.1610) the mistress of Maurice of Nassau, Prince of Orange, with whom she had 3 sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Willem of Nassau, lord of the Lek
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis of Nassau, lord of den Lek and Beverweerd
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice of Nassau
2 CONT
2 CONT Though Maurice refused to marry her (probably because she was a Catholic and only from the minor nobility), he did threaten to do so from his death bed (and to legitimise and marry off their bastard children). This would threaten 
2 CONC his half-brother Frederick Henry's place in the succession and so Frederick Henry summoned Amalia of Solms-Braunfels and married her a few days before Maurice's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]External links
2 CONT
2 CONT Portrait in the Digitaal Vrouwenlexicon
