1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Ernst,_Duke_of_Brunswick-Dannenberg
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00010562&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Julius Ernst of Braunschweig-Dannenberg (1571-1636) was a son of Henry III, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg and Ursula of Sachsen-Lauenburg. On his father's death in 1598 he inherited the duchy of Dannenberg. He died without male issue
2 CONC  and so the duchy and his share of Hitzacker was inherited by his brother Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT He married twice, firstly to Maria of Ostfriesland (1 January 1582 - 9 July 1616), daughter of Edzard II.. They had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigismund Heinrich (30 August 1614–1 November 1614) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Katharina (9 July 1616–1 July 1665), married Adolf Friedrich I. of Mecklenburg-Schwerin (1588–1658). 
2 CONT
2 CONT On his first wife's death in 1616, he remarried to Sybille of Braunschweig-Lüneburg (3 June 1584–5 August 1652), daughter of Wilhelm von Braunschweig-Lüneburg. They had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT August (* 1619) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Maria (* 1622) 
