2 CONT Maria Belgica of Portugal, also known as Maria Belgica of Crato (born before 12 October 1598[1] – 28 July 1647), was the daughter of Manuel of Portugal, son of the self-proclaimed Portuguese king António of Crato, and Countess Emi
2 CONC lia of Nassau (1569–1629), the youngest daughter of William of Orange.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Belgica_of_Portugal
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Belgica married Colonel Theodor Croll (died 1640 in Venice - stabbed to death), Quartermaster general of Odoardo Farnese, Duke of Parma, in June 1629. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue	
2 CONT # Bern Theodore Croll 
2 CONT # Emilia Catharina Croll 
2 CONT # Anna Rosine Croll 
2 CONT # Mauritius Sabine Croll
2 CONT # Helene Beatrix Croll
2 CONT # Susanne Sidonia Croll
