2 TITL Frederick V, Elector of Palatine
2 NOTE Frederick V, Elector Palatine: 
3 CONT
3 CONT 1596–1632, king of Bohemia (1619–20), elector palatine (1610–20) as Frederick V. The Protestant diet of Bohemia deposed the Roman Catholic King Ferdinand (Holy Roman Emperor Ferdinand II) and chose Frederick as king. Influenced by
3 CONC  his minister Christian of Anhalt, Frederick accepted but did not receive the aid expected from his father-in-law, James I of England, and from the Protestant Union against Ferdinand. After initial success, his supporters were rou
3 CONC ted at White Mt. (1620). 
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Frederick in his profile.
