1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopold_Wilhelm,_Margrave_of_Baden-Baden
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrave Leopold Wilhelm of Baden-Baden (September 16, 1626 – Baden-Baden, March 1, 1671) was an Imperial Field Marschal.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of Wilhelm, Margrave of Baden-Baden and Catharina Ursula von Hohenzollern–Hechingen.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Reichs-generalfeldmarschall in 1664, he fought against Sweden in Pomerania and against the Turks in Hungary. He was Governor of Warasdin in Croatia.
2 CONT
2 CONT As his elder brother Ferdinand Maximilian of Baden-Baden, he died before his father and never ruled Baden-Baden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Leopold Wilhelm von Baden married firstly in 1659 with Anna Silvia Caretto, Countess of Millesimo (1607- February 26, 1664). They had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly he married on February 23, 1666 with Countess Maria Franziska von Fürstenberg-Heiligenberg (May 18, 1633 - March 7, 1702), daughter of Ernst Egon VIII, Count of Fürstenberg-Heiligenberg.
2 CONT  They had 6 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT  1.Leopold Wilhelm (January 20, 1667 - April 11, 1716) Rastatt
2 CONT
2 CONT  2.A son (January 20, 1677 - January 20, 1677)
2 CONT
2 CONT  3.Karl Friedrich Ferdinand (September 14, 1668 - September 14, 1680)
2 CONT
2 CONT  4.Katharina Franziska (died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT  5.Henriette died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT  6.Anna (died young)
