1 NOTE !CHRIS - THE PALATINE FAMILIES OF NEW YORK 1710 by Henry Z. Jones, Jr. p. 1135
2 CONT Johann Martin, bpt. 17 Dec 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT !CONFIRM - Ibid - He was confirmed in 1682 and was a communicant at Kettenbach
2 CONT in 1686, 1687, 1690 and 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid He married Anna Elisabetha, d/o the late Johannes Jungel from the
2 CONT oil-mill, 11 Feb 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Martin Zerber, his wife and 4 children were on Capt. Robbert Bulman's hip
2 CONT in the 4th party of Palatines in Holland in 1709 (Rotterdam Lists).  Martin
2 CONT Zerbst aged 34, his wife and sons aged 11, 8, 4 and 2, Luth., husbandman and
2 CONT vinedressere, were in the 4th arrivals in England later that year. (London
2 CONT Lists).  Martin Zerbe of Annsberg was a soldier in 1711 (Palatine Volunteers to
2 CONT Canada).  Marte Server was naturalized 17 Jan 1715/16 (Albany Nats.)  He
2 CONT evidently married again as he was listed with wife Maria Catharina with 4
2 CONT children were at Wormsdorff about 1716/17 (Simindenger Register). -Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Zerbe and Anna Elisabetha Zerbe had 9 children including Johann Jacob.
