1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lodewijk van Nassau was born the illegitimate son of Stadtholder Maurits van Oranje and Margaret of Mechelen. In 1625, after the death of Maurits, he inherited the manor of Beverweerd, on the Kromme Rijn, and Odijk
2 CONC . After the death of his brother Willem in 1627, the manor of Lek was added. He married Isabella, Countess of Hornes, on April 7, 1630. Lodewijk made a career in the States army, distinguished himself in 1629 at the Siege of 's-He
2 CONC rtogenbosch, became colonel in 1632, commanded the Rosencrants regiment after 1635, saved the guns from the enemy near Hulst in 1640, became general in 1643. major and governor of Bergen op Zoom, and in 1658 governor of 's-Hertoge
2 CONC nbosch. In 1641 his uncle Frederik Hendrik, Prince of Orange, sent him to France to explain that the marriage of his son William to Mary Stuart was a private matter and had nothing to do with the politics of the Republic. From 166
2 CONC 0 to 1662 Louis was extra-ordinary ambassador to England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth van Horne, gravin MP
