1 OCCU Member of the House of Guelph / Prince Bishop of Osnabrück (1661) / Kurfürst von Hannover (1692), Elector of Brunswick-Lüneburg, Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg in Hannover (1679-92), cr Kurfürst von Hannover (1692-98), Elector o
2 CONC f Brunswick-Luneburg
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ernst August I von Braunschweig-Lüneburg Kurfürst zu Hannover
2 CONT *Member of the House of Guelph(Welfen).
2 CONT *He and Clara Elisabeth Weisenbuch were associated.
2 CONT *Prince Bishop of Osnabrück in 1661. 
2 CONT *Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg in 1679.
2 CONT *Herzog von Hannover in 1679.
2 CONT *Kurfürst zu Hannover in 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p10141.htm#i101403 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[https://geneall.net/en/name/3980/ernst-august-elector-of-hannover/ Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernest_Augustus,_Elector_of_Brunswick-L%C3%BCneburg Wikipedia]
2 CONT *[http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I12234&tree=2 Holbek Genealogy]
2 CONT *[http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00000193&tree=LEO Genealogics]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Duke of Braunschweig-Calenberg:''' Reign 1679 - 1698
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Johann-Friedrich-Herzog-von-Braunschweig-Calenberg/6000000005608037031 Johann Friedrich] '''Successor:''' Went to Kurhannover
2 CONT *'''Elector of  Hanover:
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' He as duke '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/4555799 Georg I Ludwig]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He was was duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg and ruled over the Calenberg (or Hanover) subdivision of the duchy. He was appointed prince-elector, but died before the appointment became effective. He was also Prince-Bishop of Osnabrück.* 
2 CONC Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/44830572/ernst-august_i-von_braunschweig-l%25C3%25BCneburg Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 21 2021, 14:47:48 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernst August (Ernest Augustus) was born in 1629. He married Princess Sophia of the Palatinate in 1658. He became the Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg (Braunschweig-Lüneburg) in 1679 and the Elector (Kurfürst) of Hanover in 1692. He died
2 CONC  in 1698. He was the father of George I of Great Britain and Ireland.
