2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Anna of Bavaria (21 March 1551- 29 April 1608) was daughter the of Albert V, Duke of Bavaria and Anne Habsburg of Austria. Her maternal grandparents were Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor and Anna of Bohemia and Hungary (1503–
2 CONC 1547), daughter of King Ladislaus II of Bohemia and Hungary and his wife Anne de Foix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Anna married her maternal uncle, Charles II of Austria. They had fifteen children:
