1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT immigrated to New York Colony on June 13, 1710
2 CONT
2 CONT naturalized as a citizen of the American British Colonies on January 17, 1716 at Mayor's Court, Albany, Albany County, New York Colony with his father
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Surname has also been reported to be [https://www.geni.com/surnames/zerbe Zerbe].
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be between 1695 and 1700 in New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of baptism have also been (erroneously?) reported to be December 4, 1698 at Kettenbach, Aarbergen, Darmstadt, Hesse, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been (erroneously?) reported to be August 15, 1776 at an unspecified location.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/73171024
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-322292500/johann-jacob-zerbe-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 27 2021, 22:10:57
2 CONC  UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT He migrated from Germany with his parents when he was eleven years old, and arrived in New York June 13, 1710 with the rest of the Palatine migration and were soon settled at Livingston Manor.  He became a naturalized citizen on 1
2 CONC 7 January 1716 at Mayor's Court, Albany New York, with his father, Martin Server (Zerwe).
2 CONT
2 CONT
