1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:fmrNaOhru6cJ:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_Charles,_comte_d%27Aspremont-Lynden+&cd=1&hl=en&ct=clnk&lr=lang_en en.wikipedia.org...] ; 
2 CONT * Ferdinand Charles Gobert, comte d'Aspremont Lynden (1689–1772), was a soldier, who served in the Low countries for the Habsburgs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Charles d'Aspremont Lynden (see Castle of Aspremont-Lynden) served the Dutch Republic in the War of Spanish Succession as lieutenant between 1708 and 1714. During this war, he met Prince Eugene of Savoy, and entered in his s
2 CONC ervice in the Imperial Army in 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought the French on the Rhine and Moselle between 1733 and 1734, and the Turks between 1737 and 1738. In 1741, he became Feldmarschalleutnant.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the War of the Austrian Succession in 1743, he was Commandander-in-Chief of the Imperial and Piedmontese armies in Italy. He covered himself in glory, defeating the Franco-Spanish army in the Battle of Campo Santo. He disti
2 CONC nguished himself again in the Battle of Velletri (1744) and Battle of Piacenza in 1746.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1754 he became Field Marshal, and was also member of the War Council. '''In 1763 he was made a Knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece.'''
