0 @N6000000002322291673@ NOTE Though a Calvinist, George wa persuaded by his Roman Catholic adviser, Adam
1 CONT von Schwarzenberg, to stay out of the struggle between the Holy Roman emperor
1 CONT and the German Protestant princes. His neutrality won him the hostility of
1 CONT both sides. Gustavus II Adolpus of Sweden occupied Brandenburg in 1631,
1 CONT forcing the elector to join the Protestants, but after the Swedish defeat by
1 CONT an imperial army at Nordlingen in 1634, George withdrew from the conflict.
